+### Inspect and admit Host sources
+
+Every section, context, and tool schema retains the configured Loader entry that registered it as a branded `HostSourceId`. `promptAssemblySourceInventory(assembly)` returns those effective sources after scoped shadowing, tool restrictions, admission, and ordering; the association lives in a `WeakMap` and never adds fields to prompt or tool wire values. A waterfall listener's new or copied entry has the explicit unknown source, while a top-level assembly copy retains the source-bearing entries. `hostSourceIdForEntry(entry)` derives the same identity before that Loader entry mounts. `admitSources(predicate)` registers a global or scoped filter: every global and matching scope-chain predicate observes each effective candidate, all predicates run, and every predicate must accept before the contribution enters assembly. Section and context admission precedes their text providers and complete-section selection; a dynamic tool provider may supply one source per returned schema so admission remains per tool.
+
 ### Suppress runtime context
 
 `suppressRuntimeContext()` removes every dynamic runtime-context contribution for the calling scope without disabling the services that own the underlying facts; multiple suppressors compose and the effect restores context when none remains.
